{
  "id": 208263294,
  "iid": 9918,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Sharkd: Return status message on load if err!=0",
  "description": "Fixes a bug when the return value from `load_cap_file()` is nonzero.\nNo response is currently returned causing the client to hang. A non-zero\nerror code can happen for a variety of reasons, one of which is when the\nPCAP is truncated.\n\nAn error message from `cfile_read_failure_message()` is displayed on the\nconsole, but no data is returned to the RPC client.\n\nThis adds a call to `wtap_strerrror()` to look up a human consumable error\nmessage for the specific error code returned during `wtap_read()`.\n\nAdds a new self-test and truncated pcap to `suite_sharkd.py` to verify the behavior.\n\nBefore:\n```json\n{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"load\",\"params\":{\"file\": \"trunc.pcap\"}}\n\n\n```\nNo response!\n\nAfter:\n\n```json\n{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"load\",\"params\":{\"file\": \"trunc.pcap\"}}\n{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"result\":{\"status\":\"Less data was read than was expected\",\"err\":-12}}\n```\n\nIt's important to note that this should _not_ return an error code, since Sharkd is still perfectly capable of operating on a truncated file.",
  "state": "merged",
